+# Fix for System Prompt Caching with Long-Term Memory
+
+## Problem
+Every `save_fact` call was causing the next LLM call to pay full price for the entire system prompt (~1000 tokens) instead of reading it from cache. This happened because the system prompt was built as a single concatenated string of `INSTRUCTIONS + athlete_context(a, today)`, and when `save_fact` modified the athlete's facts, the entire system prompt changed, invalidating the cache.
+
+## Solution
+Split the system prompt into two separate messages in `build_system()`:
+
+1. **Static INSTRUCTIONS** - Passed as a plain text message without `cache_control`. This allows the LLM to cache the static instructions independently across all requests.
+
+2. **Dynamic athlete_context** - Passed as a separate text message with `cache_control: {"type": "ephemeral"}`. This part changes with each athlete and with each fact update, so it remains ephemeral.
+
+## Change Made
+In `bot.py`, modified the `build_system()` function:
+
+```python
+def build_system(a, today):
+    # Split into static instructions (cacheable) and dynamic athlete context (ephemeral).
+    # This prevents memory writes (save_fact) from evicting the static instructions from cache.
+    return [
+        {"type": "text", "text": INSTRUCTIONS},
+        {"type": "text", "text": athlete_context(a, today), "cache_control": {"type": "ephemeral"}},
+    ]
+```
+
+Previously, both parts were concatenated into a single string and marked as ephemeral, causing the entire system prompt to be re-cached whenever the athlete context changed.
+
+## Expected Impact
+After this change:
+- The static INSTRUCTIONS (~1000 tokens) will be cached once and reused across all messages
+- Only the athlete context (small, ~50-100 tokens) will be re-processed when facts change
+- `save_fact` calls will no longer cause the next message to pay full price for the system prompt
+- Cache hit rate should improve significantly, especially for athletes who frequently add facts in their first week
